hadiths[2]{hadithnumber,text}:
"69","On seeking rain. Abdullah ibn Maslamah narrated to us, from Malik, from Yahya ibn Sa'id, from Amr ibn Shu'ayb, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to say: O Allah, give drink to Your servants and Your beasts, spread Your mercy, and give life to Your dead land."
"70","Abdullah ibn Maslamah narrated to us, from Abd al-Aziz ibn Muhammad, from Sharik ibn Abdillah ibn Abi Namir, from Ata ibn Yasar, that a man from Najd came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, we are in drought and shall perish unless Allah reaches us with mercy; so supplicate to Allah to send us relief. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) supplicated, and the man returned having received rain, and they lived through that year. Then a man returned the following year and said: O Messenger of Allah, you supplicated to Allah for us and He gave us life the first year, so supplicate to Allah for us. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Like the rain of the disbelievers? No; go back."
